{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3Q3TBgQS5ZJ4Fx5mQMZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] `npm run test:hydration`, `npm run test:hydration-dev` and the listener test pass\n\nTicket 10 is done: all four checklist items are finished and every suite passes. The previous attempt only failed because another worktree was holding port 8123, and its commits were gone, so I redid the work. This time I checked the port was free before running `npm test`.\n\n1. **Page content comes only from state.** `heading` and `badgeLabel` are now part of the app state and its serialized form, with defaults that keep the old text. `IndexPage(state)` reads them from state, and `createApp` no longer takes the `index` options. A new test in `test/hydration.ts` checks that each response is exactly what you get by rendering that response's own serialized state. It covers `/`, `?count=12`, `/index.html`, `/list`, `/notice` and an unknown path, and passes a leftover `index` option to make sure it has no effect. The test that escaped text appears once now builds its page from state. I removed the test of the old `IndexPage(state, opts)` arguments because that API no longer exists, and the state-based test covers the same escaping.\n2. **Paths outside the prefix** now get a new not-found route, `/404`, which is not in the route table. That applies to anything not starting with `/example-hydration/`, including look-alikes such as `/example-hydrationx/...`. The test checks for a 404, that the serialized state names the not-found page, and that no nav link is marked current.\n3. **`/example-hydration/index.html`** now maps to route `/`, so the nav marks the home link as current. I removed `/index.html` from the route table.\n\nThe example README describes the new state fields and the 404 behaviour. Re-running `toc:hydration` changed nothing. I also added a short note to the hydration section of AGENTS.md.\n\n**Test results:** `test:hydration` 129 passed, plus 17 in the listener test; `test:hydration-dev` 17; `test:ssr` 112; `npm test` 413; Playwright e2e 12. Lint and both typechecks are clean.\n\nThere are four commits. My notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which isn't committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":232,"cache_read_input_tokens":79080,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":232},"output_tokens":672,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b9bec749-9245-4b93-ac6b-2988681b5d48","uuid":"e2fbc536-ff1b-4e86-8fb1-c825bf98e836","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:33:20.868Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3Q3SwJCkSQ2xp59EcYF"}
